# Memory Loop MCP Server Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Add an MCP server (`entire mcp-server`) that exposes `search_memories` and `save_memory` tools, giving Claude the ability to pull memories on demand and create new ones mid-session.

**Architecture:** New `entire mcp-server` subcommand using `github.com/mark3labs/mcp-go` (stdio transport). Two tools reuse existing `memoryloop` package functions. Hook installation extended to write `mcpServers` config into `.claude/settings.json`. In `manual` mode, MCP is the only injection path; in `auto` mode, MCP complements hook-based injection.

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.1, `github.com/mark3labs/mcp-go` (MCP server SDK), `github.com/spf13/cobra` (CLI), existing `memoryloop` package

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-03-31-memory-loop-mcp-server-design.md`

